From 8ef44d3e875c9827b30bf28134efa2c2ebdfd1c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Message-Id: <cobiplayer-9003-android-app-proxy@localhost>
From: Cobi Player <build@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:20:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] android: an app-set proxy that libVLC never connects past

Cobi Player routes only its own traffic through the user's VPN or proxy,
via an in-process gateway on 127.0.0.1 that takes a fresh login on every
start, so no other process on the device can use it. The app sets the Java
system property ch.codebits.cobiplayer.proxy to
"http://user:pass@127.0.0.1:port" and clears it for none. The Android twin
of the Apple engine's patch 0007; the parts outside src/android are 0007's
as they are. While the property is set:

- Routed (src/android/specific.c, vlc_getProxyUrl): http, https and the
  HTTP-speaking legacy schemes icyx/unsv/itpc (legacy http.c) and mmsh
  (mmsh.c) go to the proxy, before the device's own (http.proxyHost);
  https as CONNECT, the others in absolute form. A dead proxy fails them.
  Read through System.getProperty, the call specific.c already makes for
  http.proxyHost: no new JNI symbol, no libvlcjni change.
- Refused (src/input/access.c, one check in access_New): every other
  scheme except local ones (file, fd, directory, concat, data, imem, ...).
  That is the first URL and every redirect: the http module turns ICY
  answers into icyx:// and "Pragma: features" into mmsh://, and a Location
  may name rtsp, ftp, smb, ... HLS/DASH segments come through the same
  place.
- FFmpeg (modules/demux/avformat/demux.c) gets an empty protocol
  whitelist, so it can't open nested inputs (an HLS playlist's segments)
  itself.
- The login goes to the proxy as Basic Proxy-Authorization on CONNECT
  (tunnel.c; now fails the CONNECT if it can't be added) and on every
  plain-http request (connmgr.c). connmgr.c looks the proxy up once per
  request and remembers which proxy a keep-alive connection was opened
  through, so a connection from before a proxy change is dropped, not
  reused: no request goes past a newly set proxy, and the login never
  reaches an origin. A proxy URL that can't be read fails the request.
- The login never reaches the debug log: the outgoing-request lines of
  h1conn.c, legacy http.c and mmsh.c show only the request line, and
  legacy http.c no longer logs the full proxy URL.
- A bad proxy URL (not "http://[user:pass@]host:port", e.g. an unencoded
  '/' in the login, which would change the host) is replaced by a closed
  port (http://127.0.0.1:1), never by "no proxy"; so is a property that
  can't be read. Out of memory aborts rather than going direct.

Not upstream.
